WayVR's virtual output, the one screen its apps see, is 2560x1440, a
constant (WAYVR_SCREEN_RES), and it caps every panel: a window can not
be launched, resized or maximized past it, so `wayvrctl process-launch
--resolution 3840x1080` gave 2560x1080. This adds a config key,
wvr_screen_res: [w, h] (default the old size, clamped to 640x480 and
8192 a side so that a typo can not ask for an impossible texture), read
when the output is made, and a 2160p preset to the launcher, whose
presets ended at 1440p. Set it in a file of its own under
~/.config/wayvr/conf.d, e.g. { "wvr_screen_res": [6400, 2160] }.
Made against wayvr main at cc8843a (2026-11-26). Ours, not upstream.

